### Release preview handler handles

**Severity:** `medium`

Each shared preview-handler instance owns both a resize event and, after preview launch, a process handle. The destructor currently releases neither, so repeated Explorer previews leak kernel handles in the long-lived host process. Unload the child process and close the event when the COM object is destroyed.

```suggestion
PreviewHandler::~PreviewHandler()
{
    Unload();
    if (m_resizeEvent)
    {
        CloseHandle(m_resizeEvent);
    }

    InterlockedDecrement(&g_cDllRef);
}
```

### Close the completed thumbnail process handle

**Severity:** `medium`

`SEE_MASK_NOCLOSEPROCESS` returns an owned process handle. Waiting for the thumbnail generator does not release that handle, so every thumbnail request leaks one in the Explorer host. Close it immediately after the wait and clear the member before continuing.

```suggestion
m_process = sei.hProcess;
WaitForSingleObject(m_process, INFINITE);
CloseHandle(m_process);
m_process = NULL;
```
